/-!
# Hilbert–Samuel functions of formal power series ideals and lexicographic stabilization

For an ideal `I` in a formal power series ring `MvPowerSeries σ K` over a field `K` in finitely
many variables, Hironaka's formal division theorem identifies `MvPowerSeries σ K ⧸ I` as a
`K`-vector space with the subspace of series supported outside the initial diagram
`MonomialOrder.degLex.initialDiagram I` (`MonomialOrder.quotientEquivComplementSubmodule`). Passing
to `I ⊔ 𝔪 ^ (n + 1)` adjoins all exponents of total degree at least `n + 1` to the graded
lexicographic initial diagram (`MonomialOrder.initialDiagram_degLex_sup_maximalIdeal_pow`), while
local length over `MvPowerSeries σ K` agrees with `K`-vector space length because the residue field
of `MvPowerSeries σ K` is `K` (`MvPowerSeries.length_eq_length`). Consequently,
`TauCeti.localQuotientHilbertSamuel (MvPowerSeries σ K) I n` counts the exponents `α : σ →₀ ℕ` of
total degree at most `n` outside `degLex.initialDiagram I`
(`TauCeti.localQuotientHilbertSamuel_mvPowerSeries`, Bierstone–Milman 1997, Corollary 3.20). For
the zero ideal this recovers the binomial count `Nat.choose (Nat.card σ + n) (Nat.card σ)`
(`TauCeti.localQuotientHilbertSamuel_mvPowerSeries_bot`).

In fixed finite embedding dimension, any sequence of upward-closed subsets `D j ⊆ (σ →₀ ℕ)` whose
degree-bounded complement counts are lexicographically nonincreasing eventually stabilizes in those
counts (`TauCeti.exists_forall_ge_card_degree_le_notMem_eq_of_isUpperSet`). Indeed, along a
nonprincipal ultrafilter on `ℕ`, the limit upper set `Dlim = {α | ∀ᶠ j in 𝓤, α ∈ D j}` is finitely
generated by Dickson's lemma (`WellQuasiOrderedLE.finite_of_isAntichain`), so some `D j₀` contains
`Dlim`; a strict lexicographic drop from `j₀` to `j₀ + 1` at some least degree `n₁` would then
force a strict increase between `j₀ + 1` and a later `j₂` agreeing with `Dlim` up to degree `n₁`.
Applying this to graded lexicographic initial diagrams yields lexicographic stabilization
(`TauCeti.exists_forall_ge_localQuotientHilbertSamuel_eq_of_lex`, `TauCeti.hsLexStabilization`) and
hence pointwise stabilization (`TauCeti.exists_forall_ge_localQuotientHilbertSamuel_eq_of_le`,
`TauCeti.hsPointwiseStabilization`) for Hilbert–Samuel functions of ideals in `MvPowerSeries σ K`
(Bierstone–Milman 1989, Theorem 5.2.1; Bierstone–Milman–Temkin 2011, §6.1).

## Main definitions and results

* `MonomialOrder.complementSubmoduleEquivFun`: the `R`-linear equivalence between
  `ord.complementSubmodule I` and `{α : σ →₀ ℕ // α ∉ ord.initialDiagram I} → R`.
* `MvPowerSeries.length_eq_length`: for any `(MvPowerSeries σ K)`-module `M` over a field `K`,
  `Module.length (MvPowerSeries σ K) M = Module.length K M`.
* `MonomialOrder.initialDiagram_degLex_sup_maximalIdeal_pow`: over a field `K`,
  `degLex.initialDiagram (I ⊔ 𝔪 ^ k) = degLex.initialDiagram I ∪ {α | k ≤ α.degree}`.
* `TauCeti.localQuotientHilbertSamuel_mvPowerSeries`: `H_I(n)` equals the `Nat.card` of
  `{α : σ →₀ ℕ // α.degree ≤ n ∧ α ∉ degLex.initialDiagram I}`.
* `TauCeti.localQuotientHilbertSamuel_mvPowerSeries_bot`,
  `TauCeti.localQuotientHilbertSamuel_mvPowerSeries_fin_bot`,
  `TauCeti.localQuotientHilbertSamuel_mvPowerSeries_span_image_X`,
  `TauCeti.localQuotientHilbertSamuel_mvPowerSeries_span_X`,
  `TauCeti.localQuotientHilbertSamuel_mvPowerSeries_span_X_pow`: explicit evaluations for `⊥`,
  coordinate ideals `Ideal.span (X '' S)`, coordinate hyperplanes `(X i)`, and univariate monomial
  powers `(X 0 ^ k)`.
* `TauCeti.exists_forall_ge_card_degree_le_notMem_eq_of_isUpperSet`: lexicographic stabilization of
  degree-bounded complement counts for sequences of upper sets in `σ →₀ ℕ` (`[Finite σ]`).
* `TauCeti.exists_forall_ge_localQuotientHilbertSamuel_eq_of_lex`,
  `TauCeti.hsLexStabilization`,
  `TauCeti.exists_forall_ge_localQuotientHilbertSamuel_eq_of_le`,
  `TauCeti.hsPointwiseStabilization`: lexicographic and pointwise stabilization of realized
  Hilbert–Samuel functions in `MvPowerSeries σ K` and `MvPowerSeries (Fin n) K`.

## References

* Edward Bierstone and Pierre D. Milman, *Uniformization of analytic spaces*, J. Amer. Math. Soc.
  2 (1989), 801–836, Theorem 5.2.1, pp. 820–821.
* Edward Bierstone and Pierre D. Milman, *Canonical desingularization in characteristic zero by
  blowing up the maximum strata of a local invariant*, Invent. Math. 128 (1997), 207–302,
  Corollary 3.20, p. 239, and §9, p. 276.
* Edward Bierstone, Pierre D. Milman, and Michael Temkin, *$\mathbb{Q}$-universal
  desingularization*, Asian J. Math. 15 (2011), 229–250, §6.1.
-/

